Imagine you’re discussing national priorities with friends over coffee, and the conversation turns to what this country should focus on most in the coming decade. You’re asked to choose just one priority as the most important, and a second as the next most important, from the following four options:  
(1) Achieving strong economic growth;  
(2) Building up robust national defense capabilities;  
(3) Empowering people to have greater voice and influence in decisions at work and in their local communities;  
(4) Enhancing the beauty and livability of our cities and natural landscapes.  
Which would you pick as your top priority, and which as your second?
